Hello, and welcome to this module which will introduce you to one of the key engineering

2
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:23,680
controls. Biological safety cabinets offer a safe working environment in which both

3
00:00:23,680 --> 00:00:31,960
the operator as well as the sample are protected from extraneous contamination. This biological

4
00:00:31,960 --> 00:00:39,280
safety cabinet must be utilized in accordance with the administrative control for the standard

5
00:00:39,280 --> 00:00:47,160
operating procedures stated therein. Every biological safety cabinet must be certified

6
00:00:47,160 --> 00:00:54,800
periodically in compliance with your local regulatory authority or your national standards.

7
00:00:54,800 --> 00:01:01,260
The biological safety cabinet must be utilized in accordance with the standard operating

8
00:01:01,280 --> 00:01:10,310
procedure in order to achieve a safe and conducive working environment. As we proceed in this

9
00:01:10,310 --> 00:01:17,290
module, I will introduce you to the standard operating procedures for this particular biological

10
00:01:17,290 --> 00:01:24,250
safety cabinet. Please take note that the procedures may vary based on the manufacturer

11
00:01:24,250 --> 00:01:31,610
and you will have to develop your own standard operating procedures and validate them prior to

12
00:01:31,610 --> 00:01:43,340
commencing operations in biological safety cabinets. In this video, I will be describing

13
00:01:43,340 --> 00:01:51,460
to you the layout of the standard biological safety cabinet. This cabinet is designed to

14
00:01:51,460 --> 00:02:02,510
protect both the sample as well as the operator from exposure to the biological agent. As you

15
00:02:02,510 --> 00:02:10,690
can see, all your equipment within this biological safety cabinet has to be laid out so as to

16
00:02:10,690 --> 00:02:18,990
ensure a smooth working environment. These are the pipettes which are required for dispensing

17
00:02:18,990 --> 00:02:27,710
the samples which are located at this end. These are my pipette tips. This is the sample

18
00:02:27,710 --> 00:02:34,150
which will be transferred and finally over here, I have the waste container. This waste

19
00:02:34,150 --> 00:02:41,910
container is specially designed for sharps and other disposable waste. For the purpose

20
00:02:41,910 --> 00:02:49,630
of our biological safety cabinet, pipette tips are considered as sharps and are disposed

21
00:02:49,630 --> 00:02:57,910
in this container. The container is filled to one-fourth of its level with a designated

22
00:02:57,910 --> 00:03:11,660
stirrullant. In this case, I am using 70% ethanol. When we work, we generally work in

23
00:03:11,660 --> 00:03:20,420
a smooth flow. So as you can see, I am going to select the pipette. Then I install the pipette

24
00:03:20,420 --> 00:03:37,040
tip. I set the volume and I am going to withdraw the sample from this bottle and dispense it

25
00:03:37,040 --> 00:03:59,840
in the appropriate slot. This is smooth operation of the entire process. When you complete dispensing

26
00:03:59,840 --> 00:04:14,000
the sample, the tips can be disposed in the waste container. There are some tips which

27
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:22,160
one needs to note when working in this biological safety cabinet. This region basically has a

28
00:04:22,160 --> 00:04:29,240
downdraft of air which protects me as the operator from this sample as well as protects

29
00:04:29,240 --> 00:04:36,480
the sample from any kind of contamination which may be produced in the environment. Which

30
00:04:36,480 --> 00:04:45,040
is why we work within this zone. There are some things which you cannot do in a biological

31
00:04:45,040 --> 00:04:52,240
safety cabinet. For example, the usage of open flames is not permitted as the flame

32
00:04:52,240 --> 00:04:59,480
will generate a convection current which can disturb the flow of air in this biological

33
00:04:59,480 --> 00:05:06,840
safety cabinet. The second thing which you cannot do is operate centrifuges in this environment

34
00:05:06,840 --> 00:05:14,600
as centrifuges have their own specific air flow patterns generated by their cooling motors

35
00:05:14,600 --> 00:05:20,960
and this can in turn disturb the air flow. These are some of the precautions which

36
00:05:20,960 --> 00:05:27,040
you need to take into consideration when working in a biological safety cabinet. Now biological

37
00:05:27,040 --> 00:05:35,840
safety cabinets must be decontaminated prior to use using a specified sterilizing agent

38
00:05:35,840 --> 00:05:46,790
as well as ultraviolet light and disinfected post usage by using the same sterilant. With

39
00:05:46,790 --> 00:05:54,390
regard to clean up of this cabinet after use, please ensure that you dispose of this

40
00:05:54,390 --> 00:06:02,110
waste bin in a designated area and in accordance with the requisite standard operating procedure

41
00:06:02,110 --> 00:06:08,950
when it achieves a level which is two-thirds full. This bin has to be sealed and disposed

42
00:06:08,950 --> 00:06:18,150
of according to the standard operating procedure which may involve autoclaving or incineration.

43
00:06:18,150 --> 00:06:26,870
These are some of the basic guidelines for utilizing a biological safety cabinet. Please

44
00:06:26,870 --> 00:06:33,830
